WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:15.180
12. You are what you eat. Ancient medical traditions often focus on food. After all, what we put into our body must affect how our body feels.

2
00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:23.180
But what about our minds? Does what we eat affect how we feel and think? Recent research says yes.

3
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:31.180
Different foods affect different hormones in our brains. Fruits and vegetables generally increase hormones that make us calm.

4
00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:36.180
Foods with a lot of protein, on the other hand, increase hormones that make us alert.

5
00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:46.180
But junk food, fatty, salty, sugary food without much nutrition, has a negative effect. It can make us tired and stressed.

6
00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:55.180
Different ingredients in junk food have different effects. One very important and unhealthy ingredient in junk food is trans fat.

7
00:00:55.180 --> 00:01:05.180
Trans fats are types of fat often found in junk food. Doctors have been studying the effects of trans fats recently, and the results aren't good.

8
00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:16.180
Trans fats seem to be linked to poor memory and depression. An American study found that people remembered fewer words from a list after eating trans fats than before.

9
00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:23.180
Meanwhile, a study in Spain found that eating a lot of trans fats caused people to become depressed.

10
00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:33.180
Doctors don't fully understand why these things happen. Trans fats seem to slow down our normal brain function, making us forgetful.

11
00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:42.180
They also appear to lower serotonin, our body's mood-balancing chemical, making us sad, angry, or even violent.

12
00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:49.180
But the bad news about junk food is good news about healthy food. Eating well, it seems, can make us happier.

13
00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:57.180
So, if you're feeling blue, don't reach for a bag of potato chips. They may make you feel good for the moment, but bad in the long run.
